# Podfile.lock is intentionally untracked here — this repo's iOS pods can
# only actually be resolved with a real CocoaPods/Xcode toolchain, which
# isn't available in every environment that edits this codebase. A
# committed-but-stale lock file (missing pods for a newly added plugin) is
# worse than none: Xcode's "[CP] Check Pods Manifest.lock" build phase
# fails outright if Podfile.lock and Pods/Manifest.lock disagree, which is
# exactly what happened here. ci_post_clone.sh's `pod install` always
# resolves fresh in CI instead. If you have CocoaPods locally and want
# reproducible/pinned pod versions, remove this ignore rule and commit a
# real `pod install`-generated Podfile.lock yourself.
Podfile.lock

# Exceptions to above rules.
!default.mode1v3
!default.mode2v3
!default.pbxuser
!default.perspectivev3
